{"id": "q0035", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 4030272004, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "Louise is an artist and needs to apply a coat of varnish to her latest paintings. Usually it takes 7 minutes for the coat of varnish to dry on one painting. However, today she is using a new varnish and it takes 12 minutes for the coat to dry. How much longer will it take for the coat of varnish on 6 paintings with the new varnish to dry as it would with the old varnish?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0035.wav", "input_sha256": "f84b5f0dca9a1e6009f5429cac4062df2e8b4a6650d730b6451293a1e9550f2e", "input_samples": 442400, "input_s": 27.65, "n_real_chunks": 28, "score": 0.2158, "act": 0.9994, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So the old varnish takes 7 minutes per painting. For six paintings, that would be 6 times 7, which is 42 minutes total. The new varnish takes 12 minutes per painting. For six painting s, that's 6 times 12, equal ing 7 2 minutes total. To find out how much longer it takes with the new varnish, we subtract the old time from the new time: 7 2 minus 42 equals 30 minutes. So it will take 3 0 minutes longer for the new varnish to dry on six painting s compared to the old one.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 27, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 34, "feed_lag_max_ms": 66, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 77, "audio_files"