{"id": "q0051", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2702078363, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "Gary bought a boat for $9000.  Over the first year it depreciated 30%.  The second year it depreciated another 30%.  The third year it depreciated 20%.  How much is the boat worth after the three years?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0051.wav", "input_sha256": "ed2b21ccc3a8461b463e87de9cc78c3e895033650ae31f50c1477c319fb7f2ec", "input_samples": 274800, "input_s": 17.175, "n_real_chunks": 18, "score": 0.2257, "act": 0.9989, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So Gary bought a boat for $9, 000. In the first year it depreci ated 30%, so that means it lost 30% of its value. That's 9,00 0 times 0.3 is 2, 70 0. So after the first year it' s worth 9,000 minus 2,700 which is 6 3 0 0. Then in the second year it depreciated another 30%, but now we're taking 30% off of 6,3 00. So that's 6,3 00 times 0. 3 which is 1,8 90. So after the second year it' s worth 6, 300 minus 1,890 which is 4,4 10. Then in the third year it depreciated another 2 0%, so we take 20% off of 4,410. So that's 4,4 10 times 0. 2 which is 8 82. So after the third year it's worth 4,41 0 minus 8 82 which is 3,5 28. So the boat is worth 3,5", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 17, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 60, "feed_lag_max_ms": 150, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 243, "aud