{"id": "q0360", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 4284656791, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "\"After stints backing Little Richard and the Isley Brothers, who was discovered leading \"\"Jimmy James and the Blue Flames\"\" at the Caf Wha? in New York and taken to London on 26 September 1966 to make hit records?\"", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0360.wav", "input_sha256": "2a29be8bee34166697c3af7ae7d6e5c84573b0a55dbf7e1ed81bd902b1935224", "input_samples": 231800, "input_s": 14.488, "n_real_chunks": 15, "score": 0.8925, "act": 0.9996, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "That would be Billy Preston. He was the keyboardist for Little Richard, and he also played with The Iley Brothers. And then he discovered Jimmy James and the Blue Flames at the Cafe Wha, which is where he saw them perform. And then he took them to London on September 2 6th, 19 66 to make hit records.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 14, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 24, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0360_conservative_local.wav", "sha256": "66a1ab42258f90e4ea44f97b08a55d2576e357970c5530795958246760e567b3", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 23.8}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.087, 1.159, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.096, 2.172, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.107, 3.189, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.091, 4.165, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.096, 5.173, 1, 0,