{"id": "q0382", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2414862389, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "In the very first Boston Marathon, 15 runners competed. How many finished?", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0382.wav", "input_sha256": "18870eefe6c2fb40a6644492175c05c29787af73df0f331bb3823dd86482df96", "input_samples": 78600, "input_s": 4.912, "n_real_chunks": 5, "score": 0.7696, "act": 0.9983, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "That's a really good question. I don't know the exact answer, but it was probably around 1 0 or so. It was definitely less than half of them finished the race because they were running on dirt roads and there wasn' t much support out there for them at all. So I would say maybe between five to ten people actually completed the race.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 5, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 22, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0382_conservative_local.wav", "sha256": "e7c9873f70ba6e580cec4ef2ddcaf27091471f03be7e880bd264466169199480", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 22.08}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.084, 1.151, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.083, 2.148, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.081, 3.146, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.084, 4.151, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 4.912, 4.999, 5.066, 1, 0, 0], [5, 0, 5.912, 5.998, 6.592, 0, 24000, 0], [6, 0, 6.912, 6.999, 7.835, 0, 24000, 0], [7, 0, 7.912, 7.998, 8.83,